    "body": "﻿Batch gate (`cargo xtask gate batch`, Windows, head 9e1859e4, own worktree/target; run because the diff touches Cargo.lock):\n- geometry, cl, tools, post, sim, motion: ok - 1185 passed, 0 failed (tools: 38 lib + 3 `catalog_asset_tests`).\n- app: 1713 passed, **1 failed** - `fixture_library::the_library_folder_is_the_override_else_a_sibling_of_machines` (`user_dir_for(\"macos\", CAMCRAFT_FIXTURES=/shop/fixtures)` -> None). This is the known Windows-only path bug #723 (Unix-style paths aren't absolute on Windows), not touched by this PR.\n- ui: the gate's build hit a Windows paging-file limit (os error 1455) compiling after the app suite; rerun with `-j 2` (CWD crates/ui): 562 passed, 0 failed, 5 ignored (snapshots).\n- clippy `-D warnings`, all targets, every product crate: clean.\n\nPinning tests all pass: `the_shipped_asset_parses_and_every_tool_is_valid`, `the_json_catalog_keeps_the_old_tables_values`, `a_bad_catalog_is_a_named_error_not_a_panic`, `tool_library::the_shipped_catalog_asset_reads_the_same_through_the_library_reader`.\r\n",
